    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26319" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lĕpuscŭlus</span></b>  (contr. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>acc. plur.</i>
			lepusclos, Poët. ap. <i><span class="en">Lampr. Alex.
				Sev. 38</span></i>), m.
			dim.
			lepus, <i>a young</i> or <i>little hare, leveret, a hare</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in qua (insula) lepusculos vulpeculasque saepe
					vidisses,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					N. D. 1, 31, 88</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col.
				9, 9 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 4, 21, §
		47</span></i>.</div>
